## Fix
1. Observability (single owner): the framework's termination reporting already emits `ZLINK_FRAMEWORK_TERMINATION outcome= reason=`; extend that
   same emission (or its flow event) with the teardown failure's exception type/message and the stage (spot close / instance close / channel /
   context) — one place, no new logger. Parity: dotnet logs `termination_changed ... reason=` plus the exception; node reports the error in the
   shutdown outcome — match the information content.
2. Root-cause the courier-session failure (suspects: STREAM session close with bound Actor sessions at HostShutdown, binding token teardown order,
   context close after the pump fix, authority Delete/capacity contention as in dotnet B3) and fix at the owner with a regression test.

